spes: /dev/redwood-haptic, the motor for iOS's haptics (0199, spesvib=5).

iOS plays its haptics as audio on the "Actuator" device; HackiOS's HAL plug-in (userland/src/
audio_plugin.c, MIT) writes those 16-bit mono samples to /dev/redwood-haptic. With spesvib=5 the PM6125
LPG is set up once exactly as stage 4 (0192/0193: allow-listed SID 1 registers, every write read back)
and left on; the motor then follows GPIO 36. A write whose peak is above 1200/32767 keeps the motor on
for 30 ms more; a kernel thread switches GPIO 36 every 4 ms. At most 1000 ms on in one stretch, then
1000 ms off. If the LPG setup fails, no node is made and nothing is ever switched on.

